1.7.1: motion taxonomy - counterfactuals disclosed, not enforced

Movie cameras sort into three tiers: motion-native (super8,
technicolor-3strip), motion-plausible (the 35mm family), and
motion-counterfactual (toy-camera-120, disposable-flash,
midcentury-rangefinder, autochrome - never advanced a frame in
history). superjuice keeps refusing only instant cameras, where the
output medium itself cannot do motion; counterfactuals now roll with a
one-line note that they are imaginary movie cameras wearing their
stills optics. History gets a footnote, physics keeps its veto,
imagination keeps its keys. README documents the tiers; the movie
suite asserts the note fires for counterfactuals and stays quiet for
motion-native cameras.
